     "title_html": "The roles at a bud bar event",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "html": "<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Role</th><th scope=\"col\">What they do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Event lead</th><td>Runs the day: client and planner contact, venue check-in, timeline, staff breaks, and any incident decisions</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Certified server</th><td>Staffs the bar, educates guests, paces service, and watches for guests who have had too much</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Check-in / ID support</th><td>Confirms guest age before service <mark class=\"verify\">[PHILIP TO VERIFY — ID rules vary by state]</mark></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Setup and runner</th><td>Loads in, sets up, restocks supplies, and breaks down</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>At small events one person can cover two roles. The event lead role is never optional.</p>"
      }
     ]
